<%# locals: (message:, owner:, namespace:, count:) %>
<%# Broadcast to the owner's mailbox list when a reply lands in the thread
    +message+ (PersonMessage#announce_reply): its row as the owner now
    sees it, and the Unread tab's count. The row is morphed where it is,
    never moved or added, since the broadcast cannot know which folder or
    search each page shows; a page not listing it has no target, and Turbo
    skips the stream. Morphed, its link stays the same node, so the reader's
    focus stays on it (review finding 14). For the same reason its link carries
    no folder or search, and no mark: review_pane_controller keeps the open
    row's (keepMark). %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace dom_id(message, :conversation), method: :morph,
                         partial: "common/messages/conversation_summary",
                         locals: { message:, owner:, namespace:, folder: nil } %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace "messages-unread-count", messages_unread_badge(count) %>
